XQUEST-SDL — License
====================

Original game
-------------
XQuest is Copyright (C) 1994, 1995, 1996 Mark Mackey. All rights reserved.

The original XQuest game, its source code, graphics, sounds, levels, and all
other assets were created by Mark Mackey and released as shareware. The
original license (LICENSE.DOC in the xquest source tree) permits free
distribution of the unmodified game and explicitly anticipated a future
open source release of the source code.

This project (xquest-sdl) is an unofficial, non-commercial port of XQuest to
modern Linux using C and SDL2. It is offered in the spirit of the original
release: free to use and share, not for sale, with full credit to the original
author.

Conditions inherited from the original license
-----------------------------------------------
- This software may not be sold or bundled with commercial hardware or
  software without the express written permission of Mark Mackey.
- All distributions must retain this license and attribution to Mark Mackey
  as the original author of XQuest.

New code (the SDL port layer)
-----------------------------
The porting work in this repository — the C source files, build system, and
any new tooling — is released under the same non-commercial, attribution
terms as the original game. You are free to study, modify, and redistribute
it provided that:

1. Mark Mackey is credited as the original author of XQuest.
2. Any distribution makes clear this is an unofficial port and not an
   original work of the distributor.
3. No money is charged for the software beyond a reasonable media or
   distribution fee (consistent with the original shareware terms).

Disclaimer
----------
This software is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. The authors of
the port make no warranty as to its quality, performance, or fitness for any
purpose, and shall have no liability for any damages arising from its use.
